After reviewing design files for this solution I find the layout, text, and buttons of the windows forms are well thought out and easy to read. 
I especially like the simple layout of the forms. Unfortunately while this program does work it does not have the sorting and filtering options 
present for further review. In the .cs files I see good method layouts and use of Linq, just not the methods for sorting/filtering. I like the 
amount of comments present in the .cs files and the inclusion of name, assignment, class, etc. that helps clarify whose project it is. What I 
would change is further setting up the forms with back color, group boxes, radio buttons, etc. then building more off of Linq. I found that Linq 
worked well for my version of the project if you want to take a look. 
